{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043868-give-me-a-murder-worthy-of-a-mystery-one-night-game-brainstorming","id":1043868,"title":"Give Me a Murder Worthy of a Mystery-One Night Game Brainstorming.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-04T23:20:49-08:00","id":1043868,"title":"Give Me a Murder Worthy of a Mystery-One Night Game Brainstorming.","content":"As title suggest. Got a Mastigos disbarred lawyer and a Moros medical examiner, finding out more as we go. Give me your best shot-I'm selling this game to people with this murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T23:41:56-08:00","id":1043874,"title":"","content":"Do you want your killer to also be a Mage? Because a Time-heavy murder mystery would be fun (i.e. the killer is the victim or the killer is dead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T23:46:11-08:00","id":1043875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043868-give-me-a-murder-worthy-of-a-mystery-one-night-game-brainstorming?p=1043874#post1043874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you want your killer to also be a Mage? Because a Time-heavy murder mystery would be fun (i.e. the killer is the victim or the killer is dead).</div> </div> </div> </div>I want the killer to be fucking weird. Like, blue book weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-05-2017, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T01:09:48-08:00","id":1043885,"title":"","content":"Anything out of the Book of Unremitting Horror is good. Fear Itself seriously has great demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T02:22:41-08:00","id":1043896,"title":"","content":"The victim was a mind mage who's alter ego grew to the point that it separated and possessed another to kill the mage. Now he hops from person to person to hamper the investigation into the murder. Just a shop off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T04:40:12-08:00","id":1043918,"title":"","content":"Vicious killings that are extremely brutal. Targets are mutilated in weird and symbolic ways. There is nothing, at least at first, that connects all of them. Large group of the victims was in the same class during their education, some of them were in the same school, but not insignificant number of them has nothing to do with that at all.<br /> What connects all of them is one person. All of the victims have wronged him in some way - bullying in the school, &quot;stealing&quot; his sweetheart, beating him at that video game, and so on. This might cover about 10 years of relationships, and murders are symbolically relevant to the act that wronged the person. <br /> However, that person is not the killer. You see, they are perfectly functional member of the society who simply endured and are now pretty happy. But they had problems sleeping, so they went to some alternative medicine person who, after few sessions of new age mumbo jumbo, gave them some sleep medicine and since then, they sleep like a baby. They wake up full of energy, are full of optimism, started dating that person they always wanted to talk with, and in general, they are finally in control of their life. <br /> The thing is, each night when they take the sleep pill, a monster made up from all their hatred, resentment and all other repressed feelings partially emerges from their mouth in order to make a proper exit by making a hole in person's belly and chest, leaves their body, kills someone who has wronged (or &quot;wronged&quot;) the sleeper in the past, takes some part of their flesh. Comes back, reenters the hole, emerges partially from the mouth, and weaves the stolen flesh to fix the exit hole it created while going for the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T05:45:17-08:00","id":1043934,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> That reminds me of a Delta Green scenario 'A Victim of the Art'. It had the same premise of something murdering people based on the irritation of someone. The major difference is that the cause is an artefact that auto-summons a giant flying monster. The person in question just happens to wear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T06:11:14-08:00","id":1043942,"title":"","content":"How about a killer who opened a guy up, put a baby inside and used occult power to make the corpse pregnant? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T06:35:32-08:00","id":1043954,"title":"","content":"The victim appears to have been mauled by a tiger. A freaking <i>tiger</i>, in the middle of his own home. Mortal authorities are baffled, as there are absolutely no tigers nearby, be they wild or kept in zoos. All their best forensics reveal that the killer is indeed a tiger, which apparently jumped out of thin air just to kill the guy and vanished just as completely, as there are no tiger tracks leading into or out of the house.<br /> <br /> The examiner detects traces of some ectoplasm in the body. He peeks at evidence from the scene, and confirms his theory about the ectoplasm being from a manifest ghost. He tries to call up the victim's ghost, but cannot find it anywhere.<br /> <br /> The lawyer sifts through past cases and sympathetic connections, and finds out that the victim's past fiancee was also eaten by a tiger in the past. In another continent. She tries to interrogate the related people, but all of their memories have been occluded.<br /> <br /> Another tiger attack occurs, but this time there's a witness. The witness has apparently gone mad, and is babbling something about a demonic tiger with two human faces protruding from its shoulders, cackling and wailing at the same time. <hr /><br /> The Truth: The <i>chang-gui</i> is the ghost of a person eaten by a tiger. The tiger and the ghosts become symbiotes of a sort. The tiger serves as an Anchor for the ghosts, and provides them with Essence with its every meal. The ghost guides the tiger to people it had a Strong connection with, out of a warped desire to reunite with them within the tiger. The more ghosts the tiger bonds with, the more intelligent it grows, and fuses with the amalgam of ghosts in a proccess not unlike Hive-Claiming. However, the tiger needs at least three hapless victims consumed to reach self-awareness and human-level intelligence, meaning that someone must be guiding the nascent monster to its full growth, making it jump across continents if needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T07:26:33-08:00","id":1043976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043868-give-me-a-murder-worthy-of-a-mystery-one-night-game-brainstorming?p=1043918#post1043918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicious killings that are extremely brutal. Targets are mutilated in weird and symbolic ways. There is nothing, at least at first, that connects all of them. Large group of the victims was in the same class during their education, some of them were in the same school, but not insignificant number of them has nothing to do with that at all.<br /> What connects all of them is one person. All of the victims have wronged him in some way - bullying in the school, &quot;stealing&quot; his sweetheart, beating him at that video game, and so on. This might cover about 10 years of relationships, and murders are symbolically relevant to the act that wronged the person.<br /> However, that person is not the killer. You see, they are perfectly functional member of the society who simply endured and are now pretty happy. But they had problems sleeping, so they went to some alternative medicine person who, after few sessions of new age mumbo jumbo, gave them some sleep medicine and since then, they sleep like a baby. They wake up full of energy, are full of optimism, started dating that person they always wanted to talk with, and in general, they are finally in control of their life.<br /> The thing is, each night when they take the sleep pill, a monster made up from all their hatred, resentment and all other repressed feelings partially emerges from their mouth in order to make a proper exit by making a hole in person's belly and chest, leaves their body, kills someone who has wronged (or &quot;wronged&quot;) the sleeper in the past, takes some part of their flesh. Comes back, reenters the hole, emerges partially from the mouth, and weaves the stolen flesh to fix the exit hole it created while going for the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So why this highlights Mage strength:<br /> - It gives you a mystery that can't be solved outright by asking &quot;show me what was the last thing victim saw, oh, Mr Freddy? OK, let's arrest Mr Freddy&quot; without making these spells useless in obnoxious, frustrating way - magic can provide you with clues, but not the answers<br /> - It's pretty compact; you can make it shorter or longer by adding/removing extra victims<br /> - The main thing - the fact that each victim wronged the same person - is not something that can be divined by magic (well, not with their Arcana spread at least) and thus engages their own investigative powers while still letting them use magic as a tool to provide them with clues<br /> - Monster can be easily linked to Mind and Death Arcana, providing the players with opportunities to shine with their powers<br /> - &quot;I wish I had an invisible gun that could punish all people who wronged me&quot; is a thought very relevant to the Mage; the whole situation should give them some Wisdom to chew on<br /> - Instead of relying on physical (&quot;we need to kill it&quot;) conflict, which isn't very exciting in Mage (&quot;I use my Ruling spell to kill it in whatever dumb way my Arcanum allows, next&quot;), this places more weigh on &quot;here is a situation, figure it out&quot; and then &quot;you discovered the secret! What do you do now?&quot;. Because, indeed, what will they do with the person who half-mouth half-belly births a demon once per few nights? Will they investigate the weird occult guru who concocted the medicine? <br /> - Body horror is strong with this one. Not knowing that your hate clumsily patches up your body with remains of it's victims when you sleep is...scary. <br /> - It isn't a singular murder. Singular murders are tricky; multiple murders are better, because they allow bigger margin of error for players and make patterns easier to spot and identify.<br /> - serial killer case adds urgency. Each night they slack off, someone might be turned into a bonewrap for intestines tortilla full of bedbugs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:48:57-08:00","id":1044107,"title":"","content":"Liking WHW's thing so far.<br /> <br /> We've added probably an Obrimos plumber to the mix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T16:01:37-08:00","id":1044244,"title":"","content":"Obrimos adds two things to the equation: Forces and Prime. Prime doesn't provide much of extra investigative angle, but works perfectly as a double checker. Words of Truth shouldn't allow them to just repeat statements until they find a true one, but I personally allow it to &quot;say it in red&quot; when a player formed a theory they can backup with evidence and truly believe it works. This is pretty good way to keep the plot moving, as it allows an &quot;outside confirmation&quot; of players theory without relying on NPCs and undermining their own hard work; it's basically an ability to make sure that you are on good track. <br /> If murders are symbolic, Prime could give some insight into symbolism in the crime scene. Again, no direct answer, but things like &quot;This has Revenge and Broken Heart written all over it&quot;. <br /> <br /> Forces give you access to internet. Have you played Read Only Memories? Your companion, robot child Turing, can instantly scan this world's equivalent of Internet to look for specific data and do background searches of concepts and people. This is a pretty amazing ability for this kind of investigation, because it allows players to get super quick access of things like &quot;Hey Plumber Bob, can you check if anything connects them?&quot; &quot;Let me get my phone, BZZZZZZZZZZT, whoa, check it out, a lot of them went to the same class, it's all on their Facebook feed&quot;. This really helps with one-shot nature of the game in question (I think?), because it bypasses a lot of legwork to get that data, and again, it's child's play for Obrimos to get into confidential databases. And of course, without Fate, your Obrimos won't be able to just say &quot;I google search person responsible for this murder using Lucky Guess function of the google search&quot;; you just give them a tool to ask questions, but they need to formulate good questions in order to get a good answer.<br /> Honestly, Mage investigations are often Games of 20 Questions but prettied up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T16:42:40-08:00","id":1044273,"title":"","content":"-A serial killer mage is invading people's minds and stealing their memories, slowly assembling an identity for themselves after they were mind-wiped. They aren't /killing/ them, they're leaving them with a total loss of self. They keep hunting because the memories always fade with time.<br /> <br /> -A cursed mirror in a museum spawns a doppleganger every New Moon that targets the last person to look at it and kill them, and then the doppleganger takes their place.<br /> <br /> -A really weird death...like, all the bugs in an area go berserk and kill somebody and baffle witnesses.<br /> <br /> Just a few random ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11482-andar90","name":"andar90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T17:48:20-08:00","id":1044299,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't put Mages and other things like that into a mystery like this. This game should be like a pilot episode of TV series; a strong, simple, stand alone story presenting attractive qualities of the game, without drowning players in complicated jargon and other setting mastery elements. It also should be a closed, self contained story, which has potential to lead into something else. In case of my example, you have a unique monster that doesn't really map towards the rest of CofD ecosystem, which makes it relatively easy to understand within the context of the story without system/game mastery knowledge and without slowing down the play to introduce concepts like Ghosts or Goetia. You want the players to feel free thinking about outstandish stuff, not make them feel like there is a complicated encyclopedia of ephemeral monsters in the back of the book that they are supposed to memorize in order to play the game properly.<br /> <br /> It's also good to estabilish 3 phases of play: Investigative Phase, &quot;Deal With Monster of The Week&quot; Phase, ending with &quot;How do we fix the damage this did?&quot; Phase. Investigative Phase relies heavily on Knowing and Unveiling Spells, which are pretty simple to wrap your head around - it's basically &quot;ask a question falling within your purview!&quot;, with occasional Compelling or Ruling to unlock certain options. This provides new players with relatively safe environment to experiment with and get comfortable with their powers, which is incredibly important in Mage. &quot;Dealing with it&quot; Phase places heavier emphasis on Ruling spells, which are more complicated than Unveilings and Knowings, and require either pre-planning their use, or good eye for opportunity. Consequences Phase requires most complicated and sophisticated uses of Magic - which in turn requires experience and confidence. These require actual practice; this comes last in hope that all of the previous phase will build up enough confidence in the players to actually try out some out of the box solutions to the problems that require using Weaving, Perfecting and Fraying. Note that Magic is bad at permanently solving solutions without destroying things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T16:10:17-08:00","id":1044760,"title":"","content":"Way back when TSR/Wizards released a game called Alternity/Dark Matter (think X-Files) and with it a demo adventure named 'Exit some number'. It began with the characters being trapped with several strangers in a truck stop by a winter storm, than a man's body was discovered in the men's room. Said man was transporting an imprisoned Winter spirit but among the other stragglers are a couple of evil cultists who murdered him, released the Winter spirit and intend to sacrifice everyone at the truck stop to it.<br /> \u200bThe murder was relativley straight forward but with the added difficulty of a spirit actively working to kill everyone while the heroes had to retrieve its prison from the cultists.<br /> It would require conversion to CofD but the basic idea might be useful and having been a free demo you could probably still find it on the net.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T21:26:36-08:00","id":1046169,"title":"","content":"So, did this game happen? I'm interested in how it went. I also can give out more Mage-specific advice, as this game kinda has special needs when introducing it to new people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T01:09:23-08:00","id":1046206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043868-give-me-a-murder-worthy-of-a-mystery-one-night-game-brainstorming?p=1043918#post1043918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicious killings that are extremely brutal. Targets are mutilated in weird and symbolic ways. There is nothing, at least at first, that connects all of them. Large group of the victims was in the same class during their education, some of them were in the same school, but not insignificant number of them has nothing to do with that at all.<br /> What connects all of them is one person. All of the victims have wronged him in some way - bullying in the school, &quot;stealing&quot; his sweetheart, beating him at that video game, and so on. This might cover about 10 years of relationships, and murders are symbolically relevant to the act that wronged the person.<br /> However, that person is not the killer. You see, they are perfectly functional member of the society who simply endured and are now pretty happy. But they had problems sleeping, so they went to some alternative medicine person who, after few sessions of new age mumbo jumbo, gave them some sleep medicine and since then, they sleep like a baby. They wake up full of energy, are full of optimism, started dating that person they always wanted to talk with, and in general, they are finally in control of their life.<br /> The thing is, each night when they take the sleep pill, a monster made up from all their hatred, resentment and all other repressed feelings partially emerges from their mouth in order to make a proper exit by making a hole in person's belly and chest, leaves their body, kills someone who has wronged (or &quot;wronged&quot;) the sleeper in the past, takes some part of their flesh. Comes back, reenters the hole, emerges partially from the mouth, and weaves the stolen flesh to fix the exit hole it created while going for the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love it! I will use it as an adventure for my group! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T10:46:15-08:00","id":1049929,"title":"","content":"Victim was shot, witnesses heard the shot, nobody saw a shooter. Despite the impossibility of it, all forensic evidence points to the bullet have originated <b>within </b>the victim's chest cavity, piercing the heart from the inside out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 02-16-2017, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}